---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="∮"
  description="You found the contour integral."
  noindex
>
  <section class="section section--flush found grid-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">You clicked the little symbol</p>

      <h1 class="display found__title">∮ A·dl</h1>

      <p class="comment found__note">
        the one thing on this site that isn't about insurance
      </p>

      <div class="found__body">
        <div class="prose prose--tight">
          <p>
            That's a contour integral — you add something up all the way around a closed loop and
            come back to where you started. For three years it was most of my life.
          </p>
          <p>
            Send an electron around a loop with a magnetic field sealed inside, where the electron
            never goes. Classically nothing should happen: no field where the particle is, no force,
            no effect. It happens anyway. The electron picks up a phase shift proportional to that
            integral, and you can see it in the interference pattern.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>The field is zero everywhere the electron travels. It still knows the solenoid
            is there.</strong> That's the Aharonov–Bohm effect, and I spent those years trying to
            simulate the molecular version of it faster than anyone had managed.
          </p>
          <p>
            I left before writing up the thesis. The physics is still lovely.{' '}
            <a class="link" href="/forum_EP.pdf">The readable version is here (PDF)</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure class="diagram">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 200 160" role="img" aria-label="An electron path looping around a solenoid that carries a magnetic field confined inside it.">
            <!-- the loop the electron takes -->
            <circle class="loop" cx="100" cy="76" r="52" />
            <!-- direction of travel -->
            <path class="tip" d="M148 62 L152 76 L138 78" />
            <!-- the solenoid: field lives only in here -->
            <circle class="core" cx="100" cy="76" r="13" />
            <text class="glyph" x="100" y="82" text-anchor="middle">B</text>
            <text class="note" x="100" y="150" text-anchor="middle">field: inside only</text>
            <text class="note" x="100" y="18" text-anchor="middle">electron: outside only</text>
          </svg>
          <figcaption class="comment">no field on the path. phase shift anyway.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <p class="found__more">
        While you're here: there are two more. One wants{' '}
        <span class="mono found__keys">↑↑↓↓←→←→BA</span>. The other wants three fast clicks on any
        big heading — including the one above.
      </p>

      <div class="found__actions">
        <a class="arrow-link" href="/"><span>Back to the actual site</span><span>→</span></a>
        <a class="arrow-link" href="/about"><span>About</span><span>→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .found {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem) clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem);
  }

  .found__title {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 11vw, 6.5rem);
    margin: 1rem 0 1.1rem;
    font-variation-settings: 'SOFT' 60, 'WONK' 1;
  }

  .found__note {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .found__body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.4fr) minmax(14rem, 0.8fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .prose--tight {
    max-width: 54ch;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .prose--tight > * + * {
    margin-top: 1.1em;
  }

  .diagram {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .diagram svg {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 20rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 70%, transparent);
    padding: 0.5rem;
  }

  .loop {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 1.25;
    stroke-dasharray: 3 4;
  }

  .tip {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .core {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 16%, transparent);
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 1.25;
  }

  .glyph {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: var(--accent-ink);
  }

  .note {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 8px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    fill: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .diagram figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .found__more {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .found__keys {
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .found__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .found__body {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .diagram svg {
      max-width: 16rem;
    }
  }
</style>
